long. Affinity groups are generally precluded from being under the aegis of any governmental agency, and their purposes must be primarily non-commercial. Examples of affinity groups include private social clubs, fraternities, writing or reading circles, hobby clubs, and groups engaged in political activism. Affinity groups can be based on a common social identity or ideology (e.g., anarchism, conservatism), a shared concern for a given issue (e.g., anti-nuclear, anti-abortion) or a common activity, role, interest or skill (e.g., legal support, medical aid, software engineering). Affinity groups may have either open or closed membership, although the latter is far more common.","Class Name":"affinity group","Detailed Ontology":"gsso","Is Defining Ontology":true,"Mapped Term IRI":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GSSO_010121","Mapped Term Label":"affinity group","Mapped Term Ontology":"gsso","Match Type":"SEARCH_RESULT","Score":0.75,"Short Form":"GSSO_010121","Source":"Zooma","Zooma Confidence":"GOOD"},{"Class Definition":"The strength of noncovalent chemical binding between two substances as measured by the dissociation constant of the complex.","Class Name":"Affinity","Detailed Ontology":"bao","Is Defining Ontology":false,"Mapped Term IRI":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C20604","Mapped Term Label":"Affinity","Mapped Term Ontology":"bao","Match Type":"SEARCH_RESULT","Score":0.75,"Short Form":"NCIT_C20604","Source":"Zooma","Zooma Confidence":"GOOD"},{"Class Definition":"","Class Name":"Affinity Reagent","Detailed Ontology":"ncit","Is Defining Ontology":true,"Mapped Term IRI":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C94364","Mapped Term Label":"Affinity Reagent","Mapped Term Ontology":"ncit","Match Type":"SEARCH_RESULT","Score":0.75,"Short Form":"NCIT_C94364","Source":"Zooma","Zooma Confidence":"GOOD"},{"Class Definition":"A type of physical interaction evidence that depends on the strength of the interaction between two entities.","Class Name":"affinity evidence","Det